## Why This Is Asked
Tests time-expanded DP on grids for path counts with constraints.

## Key Concepts
- DP on (i,j,t) layers; space optimization; modulo arithmetic.
- Handling walls and boundary checks.

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPaths(grid, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const MOD = 1_000_000_007;
  if (grid[0][0] === 1 || grid[n-1][m-1] === 1) return 0;
  let prev = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(m).fill(0));
  prev[0][0] = 1;
  const dirs = [[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]];
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    const cur = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(m).fill(0));
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      if (grid[i][j] === 1) continue;
      for (const [dx,dy] of dirs) {
        const x = i + dx, y = j + dy;
        if (x>=0 && x<n && y>=0 && y<m && grid[x][y]===0) {
          cur[i][j] = (cur[i][j] + prev[x][y]) % MOD;
        }
      }
    }
    prev = cur;
  }
  return prev[n-1][m-1];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building a DP over subsequences with constraints, requiring a clear state definition and transition over previous indices, plus reconstruction capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with constraints
- State dp[i] and parent tracking
- Time/space analysis and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSubseqWithDiff(a, d) {
  const n = a.length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(0);
  const par = Array(n).fill(-1);
  let best = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    dp[i] = a[i];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      if (Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) <= d && dp[j] + a[i] > dp[i]) {
        dp[i] = dp[j] + a[i];
        par[i] = j;
      }
    }
    if (dp[i] > best) {
      best = dp[i];
      bestIdx = i;
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct subsequence
  const seq = [];
  let curr = bestIdx;
  while (curr !== -1) {
    seq.push(curr);
    curr = par[curr];
  }
  return { maxSum: best, subsequence: seq.reverse() };
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity
Time: O(n²) due to nested loops checking all previous indices
Space: O(n) for dp and parent arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine subarray maxima with partition DP, requiring both maximization and reconstruction of multiple intervals. It exercises careful indexing and boundary handling.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a cap k
- Precomputation of maxSub for O(1) subarray maxima
- 2D DP with reconstruction pointers
- Time/space tradeoffs and edge cases (k=0, equal values)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueWithKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const maxSub = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let m = -Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      m = Math.max(m, A[r]);
      maxSub[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let best = dp[i-1][t];
      let bestJ = -1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = maxSub[j-1][i-1] + dp[j-1][t-1];
        if (val > best) { best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best; take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const j = take[i][t];
    if (j === -1) break;
    res.push([j-1, i-1]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  res.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], subarrays: res};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a new DP angle: subarray-level min as value, exact k non-overlapping blocks, with clear reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exact block count
- Precomputation of subarray minima
- Backtracking to obtain endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Assumes A is 1-indexed, n = A.length-1, k given
function maxSumMinSubarrays(A, n, k) {
  const M = Array.from({length: n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));
  for (let l=1; l<=n; l++) {
    let m = A[l];
    for (let r=l; r<=n; r++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[r]);
      M[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const opt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      for (let l=1; l<=i; l++) {
        const cand = dp[l-1][t-1] + M[l][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; opt[i][t] = l; }
      }
    }
  }
  // backtrack for endpoints
  let i = n, t = k, blocks = [];
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = opt[i][t];
    blocks.push([l, i]);
    i = l-1; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

